rem Obtuse Angled Triangles
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=210
rem Count points B, |x| + |y| <= R,
rem for which triangle O B C is obtuse,
rem with C = (R/4, R/4); R is a
rem multiple of 8

use numbers
use sequences
use io
use cli

option R integer = 1000000000
option Chunk integer = 5000000

rem The angle is obtuse at O below the
rem line x + y = 0, at C above x + y =
rem R/2, and at B inside the circle on
rem OC as diameter. Points on the line
rem OC are degenerate. With K = R / 8
rem the circle is a^2 + b^2 < 2 K^2 at
rem the lattice point (K, K); its points
rem count by symmetry from a > b > 0.
Half = R // 2
Pts = 2 * R * R + 2 * R
Below = (Pts - 2 * Half) // 2
Below -= Half
M = R - Half
Quart = R // 4
Above = M * (R + 1) - M // 2
Above -= Half - Quart
K = R // 8
Q = 2 * K * K - 1
A = Q isqrt
A0 = (1 + (2 * Q - 1) isqrt) // 2
Gen = A0 * (A0 - 1) // 2
for L in A0 + 1 to A by Chunk
  Xs = L to (L + Chunk - 1 A min) array
  Gen += (Q - Xs * Xs) isqrt sum
end
Diag = Q // 2 isqrt
Circle = 1 + 4 * A + 4 * Diag + 8 * Gen
Circle -= (R - 1) // 4
Answer = Below + Above + Circle
Answer print
